  ],
  "details": "<p>The library is located in a private house in Assur.</p>\r\n<p><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"745\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan62_AssurPlan.png\" width=\"544\" /></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "In a private house in Assur, cut into by the excavation trench 8I, researchers found the remains of a library and an archive, consisting of at least 800 tablets, making it the largest library excavated in Assur. The library, mostly dating to the 7th century BC, belonged to a family of exorcists with ties to the A\u0161\u0161ur temple. Under the floors of most of excavated rooms in this house, researchers found brick boxes with apotropaic figurines. The library consisted mainly of incantations and prescriptions, but also prayers, lists of stones and plants for medical use, lexical lists, hemerological texts, as well as texts concerning the ruler's attitudes to the cult and of the destruction and rebuilding of Babylon; additionally, texts such as ration lists form an archive.",
